# GitHub Actions CI/CD & Automated Release Pipelines

This skill standardizes cross-platform continuous integration and automated release publishing across GitHub repositories. It provides matrix workflows to build Linux, Windows, and macOS binaries simultaneously.

---

## 🚀 1. Canonical Multi-OS Matrix Workflow (`.github/workflows/release.yml`)

```yaml
name: Cross-Platform Release

on:
  push:
    tags:
      - 'v*.*.*'

jobs:
  build:
    name: Build (${{ matrix.target.os }})
    runs-on: ${{ matrix.target.runner }}
    strategy:
      fail-fast: false
      matrix:
        target:
          - os: linux-x64
            runner: ubuntu-latest
            artifact: myapp-linux-x64.tar.gz
          - os: windows-x64
            runner: windows-latest
            artifact: myapp-win-x64.zip
          - os: macos-x64
            runner: macos-latest
            artifact: myapp-macos-x64.tar.gz

    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Build Binary
        run: |
          echo "Compiling for ${{ matrix.target.os }}..."
          mkdir -p dist && touch dist/placeholder

      - name: Upload Release Asset
        uses: softprops/action-gh-release@v2
        with:
          files: dist/*
        env:
          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
```

